  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## `+` and `==` ask an object for a primitive\n\n`[] + []` is `\"\"`. `[] == false` is `true` because both sides coerce. `{ valueOf() { return 1 } } + 1` is `2`.\n\nPrefer `===` and explicit `Number` / `String`. The Why is: the language has a ToPrimitive walk, not a moral about “empty”."
    },
